NAME
    history - display or clear command history

SYNOPSIS
    history
    history clear
    !N
    !!

DESCRIPTION
    Lists completed interactive command lines recorded in the current
    session, numbered starting at 1 (up to 500 entries). 'history clear'
    erases the recorded entries.

    At the start of a new interactive line (not inside an open block),
    '!N' re-runs history entry N and '!!' re-runs the most recent entry.
    History expansion runs before lexing, and the expanded command is
    what gets recorded. Lines inside a sourced script are not added to
    history and do not undergo '!' expansion; only the source(1) line
    itself is recorded.

EXAMPLES
    history
    !!
    !12
    history clear

EXIT STATUS
    0   History displayed or cleared, or re-run command succeeded.
    1   History expansion referenced an empty history or invalid index.

SEE ALSO
    dianash(1), source(1), tmux(1)
